think Crux-first among the three named siblings takes the hardest-solvable that opens the rest: a DISTANCE-based erode/dilate. It is the direct payoff the distance rung was built for ("the metric floor a distance-based erode/dilate ... all descend from"), a genuine algorithm, and it opens LINEAR-time true-radius morphology the disk-through-structure gather cannot match for speed.
think Reasoned the algorithm before coding. EROSION by radius r removes every foreground pixel within distance r of the background, so a pixel survives iff its chamfer distance EXCEEDS radius * dist_orthogonal (a true unit reads as 3 in the 3-4 field). DILATION runs the SAME transform on the COMPLEMENT mask (foreground/background swapped) and keeps every pixel WITHIN the threshold. One transform, two thresholds -- keep-above over the source for erode, keep-at-or-below over the complement for dilate.
think Derived the exact-duality before coding: because dilate runs the chamfer field on the complement of its input, complement(dilate(complement(A))) is precisely {p : chamfer-over-A field > threshold} = erode(A). So the two verbs are duals by construction, not coincidence -- provable byte-for-byte on the rendered binary masks. Chose to prove it in the selftest with a render-level flip_mask.
think Chose the crux proofs: the EROSION-DEFINITION (3x3 block erodes by radius 1 to its single center -- ring at chamfer 3 peeled, center at 6 kept); the TRUE-DISK payoff (a dot dilates to a PLUS, diagonals dark at chamfer 4, AND a square morphology.dilate DOES light those corners -- imported morphology just to measure the contrast, the way structure.rye imports it for general-contains-special); the DUALITY (byte-for-byte); a WIPED-LINE crux (a one-pixel line is all boundary so erode wipes it whole, contrasting zhang_suen which preserves a line -- two different questions of the same mask).
obs Compose not braid held cleanly: the rung OWNS only the radius-to-threshold scale, a complement builder (red = 255 - red flips on/off through the is_on threshold), and the keep/drop render. distance.distance_chamfer owns the transform, branch.is_on the binary meaning (the one door shared with label/distance/hitmiss/endpoints/zhang_suen), qoi the buffers. No new gather, blend, codec, or color math.
obs Edge convention inherited honestly from distance.rye: the canvas boundary is not background, so a shape flush against no in-image ground is not eroded there (the field's "no background reached" reads as dist_far, unbounded depth). Named in the module doc rather than papered over -- matches morphology.rye's own CLAMP convention.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- the duality and the true-disk geometry were traced by hand before coding. Witness tools/distance_morph_witness.rish GREEN. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living_docs_lint GREEN, living_card_ascii GREEN.
